      "explanation": "Pipeline-aware surge response: when demand growth exceeds 1.2, increase orders at all nodes to replenish pipelines, but cap increases to avoid overshoot. Node0 adds 2 if pipeline is low relative to recent demand, else 1. Node1 adds 1 if pipeline is low, else 0. Node2 adds 1 if pipeline is low, else 0. This coordinates upstream replenishment while limiting downstream backlog risk.",
      "rules": [
        {
          "when": "growth > 1.2 and pipeline < recent * 4",
          "delta": "min(2, max(0, 6 - happo))"
        },
        {
          "when": "growth > 1.2",
          "delta": "min(1, max(0, 6 - happo))"
        },
        {
          "when": "growth > 1.2 and pipeline < recent * 4",
          "delta": "min(1, max(0, 6 - happo))"
        },
        {
          "when": "growth > 1.2",
          "delta": "min(1, max(0, 6 - happo))"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}

